SOAPBOX: Going in, it was obvious this year's event would be a scoring challenge compared to recent years. 10 and 15 took a massive hit here with the declining solar cycle and K at 3-4. Plus local thunderstorms added to the QRN misery on the low bands Friday into Saturday.
SOAPBOX: Despite all the negatives, 20 saved the contest with openings all day and night to almost everywhere. Propagation on all the high bands was intriguing to say the least. I spent far too much time sifting through the noise on 10 and 15 pulling out weak mults. Yet there were some very strong spotlight signals from SA on 10 and EU on 15. It seemed those bands were open to areas where few participants showed up.
SOAPBOX: The next door neighbor installed a huge solar panel array on his roof so the increased QRN on my tribander made weak signal Qs almost impossible. The pasture rx antennas saved my bacon.
SOAPBOX: Nice to have LP1H call in with a 569 signal on 80. Was able to get Qs with everything heard or spotted there.
